{
 "source": "Faz 1b: transition solved on per-cell solid and gas flow. The bed calcines along the zone, so one scalar flow could be correct in at most one cell; Cs and m_dot_g became arrays, calcination now runs before the row assembly (the gas flow in a cell depends on it), and each face carries its own second-order correction. The CO2 leaves the solid at the local Ts and joins the gas at the same value, so the two rows cancel over the zone. transition -> burning handoff is now exact (ratio 1.00000, dT -0.00 K, was +44.9 K). Adds D11 thermal demand vs fuel supply.",
